{"name":"Compass","hex":"#8a877b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"compass","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A magnetic or electronic device used to determine the cardinal directions (usually magnetic or true north).","A pair of compasses (a device used to draw circular arcs and transfer length measurements)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To surround; to encircle; to environ; to stretch round.","To go about or round entirely; to traverse."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compass"}],"entries":[{"title":"Compass","blocks":[{"text":"A compass is a device that shows the cardinal directions used for navigation and geographic orientation. It typically consists of a magnetized needle or another element, such as a compass card or compass rose, that pivots to align itself with magnetic north. Other methods may be used, including gyroscopes, magnetometers, and GPS receivers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/2016_Busola.JPG/330px-2016_Busola.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compass","wikidata":"Q34735"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Model_Si_Nan_of_Han_Dynasty.jpg/500px-Model_Si_Nan_of_Han_Dynasty.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Model_Si_Nan_of_Han_Dynasty.jpg/500px-Model_Si_Nan_of_Han_Dynasty.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Model of a lodestone compass from Han dynasty","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AModel_Si_Nan_of_Han_Dynasty.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Walkers_compass_arp.jpg/500px-Walkers_compass_arp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/